  "summary": "Today's health-tech landscape shows several converging pressures on the system. Administrative friction remains a major focus, with multiple initiatives targeting prior authorization delays, check-in workflows, and the rising costs driven by automated denial systems that create a \"bot versus bot\" dynamic between providers and payers. Meanwhile, AI is being positioned as a solution across multiple domains—from reducing no-shows through human-supported systems to supporting public health agencies and enabling data-driven decision-making at health systems.\n\nOn the clinical side, reimbursement incentives are shifting to encourage preventive care, with Medicare proposing a 19% increase for smoking and alcohol cessation counseling. Industry consolidation continues with IKS Health acquiring TruBridge for $557 million, and specialized ventures like Juno Bio raising capital for vaginal health solutions and Hemispheric securing $52 million for an AI brain foundation model. Some clinical setbacks are notable, including GSK's chronic cough drug failing Phase 3 testing, while broader public health concerns range from medication shortages reaching 227 active cases to foodborne parasite outbreaks linked to Mexican lettuce at major restaurant chains.",
